Z||000000||88 Fiero GT Turbo||08-03-2000||04:23 PM||||I hope that someone can help.  Does anyone know what the stock injectors flow rate and if they are 27lb. 30lb. or what.  The second part of the question is what is the flow and pondage of the Tomco injectors that the Fiero Store is selling.<P>Later,<P>Jack<p>[This message has been edited by 88 Fiero GT Turbo (edited 08-03-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||AkursedX||08-03-2000||04:30 PM||||Actually I think stock injectors flow at 14.9 lbs/hour, and the tomco injectors flow at 15.9 lbs/hour||||reg||3
Z||000002||88 Fiero GT Turbo||08-03-2000||04:33 PM||||Also forgot to ask if anyone knows of a better set of injectors for the car.<P>Later,<P>Jack||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||08-03-2000||04:40 PM||||As your name states you have a turbo on the car.. are you sure your running lean? have you hooked an air/fuel monitor to it? i'd try that before throwing parts at it. you might also want to try the fuel injector controller from <A HREF="http://www.splitsec.com" TARGET=_blank>www.splitsec.com</A>   the shop i deal with has A/F monitors with duty cycle % also. this will tell you how hard your pushing your injectors... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  e-mail Ed and tell him Travis said you needed an A/F meter with duty cycle. These usefully AND sparkly light displays are only like $100 and will tell you how much work your fuel system really needs AND it will help you dial in the split sec computer too.. welcome to the forum!||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||08-03-2000||04:42 PM||||as for a better set.. the Tomoco units are ok.. some out of a camaro 305 will drop right in. I had RC injectors in my NOS charged SE. <A HREF="http://www.rceng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rceng.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||08-03-2000||05:45 PM||||I have a set from a 3.1 Beretta for sale that will drop right in and have better flow, if you want them, make me an offer. Someone here can probably give you specifics on flow and pressure.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000006||WisconsinGT||08-03-2000||10:23 PM||||I just got my injectors back from Marren. I guess my injectors where bad (Dirty). The spray patteren in three of the six where N/G. After they worked on them, I have a Max of 45.8 and a Min of 44.8. For a difference of 2.1. I guess that is good.||||reg||1
Z||000007||88 Fiero GT Turbo||08-03-2000||11:11 PM||||What is the pondage of the 305 camro and will any of the high performance camro injectors work on the Fiero fuel rallel<P><BR>Later,<BR>Jack||||reg||5
Z||000008||HYPTNOTiSE||08-04-2000||09:06 AM||||305-19lb<BR>350- 24lb<BR>Gn-30lb<BR>fiero-about 15<P>I'm going to be running a setof ford motorsports 30lb injectors in my project. i got htem for 75 bucks and they only have about 7500Miles. Got them from a friend. New they're 200 for 8, which is the cheapest source for new injectors. they're the pintle type, not the disk type. I'd rather have the disk type but for 8 30lb's for 75 bucks, "WHAT'S A BARGAIN!?"<P>Oh at this time i'm also going to use a split second A/F calibartor, it's the arc-2 the nicest one and an adjustable fuel pressure regulator. <P>In a few months i'm going to go with, Accel DFI's new setup. fully programmable. Windows based, and updated.  SWEEET!<BR><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||88 Fiero GT Turbo||08-05-2000||05:41 PM||||Ok guys are we saying that the fuel injector in the Grand National, Camaro, and Fiero are all interchangalbe????<P><BR>Later,<P>Jack||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||08-06-2000||01:09 AM||||Most of the injectors are *physically* interchangable. All different flow rates too.<P>There are several sites that list the flow rates. Somewhere....<P>Stock Fiero's are 15-16lbs depending on the way you do the math. 15lbs is close enough for government work.  The size varies all over hell depending on the application. <P>Make sure you know why you are changing the injector *size* if that is your plan.<P>More is not better in every instance....<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 08-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierocrazy||08-06-2000||01:10 AM||||i dont think they are, i use a  set of 3.8 injectors,  becareful that your resistance values arent differant, just because they fit doesnt meant hey will work, my stock 3.8 injectors flow 16 lbs||||reg||1
